{"game": "space-marine-2", "language": "english", "appid": 2183900, "month": "2025-05", "window": 1, "start_date": 1746057600, "end_date": 1746662399, "month_true_total": 1509, "quota": 5, "returned": 5, "pulled_at": "2026-09-11 02:21:46 Pacific Daylight Time", "reviews": [{"recommendationid": "194440880", "author": {"steamid": "76561198013758491", "personaname": "daskrieghuhn", "persona_status": "offline", "profile_url": "https://steamcommunity.com/profiles/76561198013758491/", "num_games_owned": 0, "num_reviews": 104, "playtime_forever": 730, "playtime_last_two_weeks": 0, "playtime_at_review": 718, "last_played": 1746888082, "avatar": "1ea7a0ce2cd3f056336309d9bb97ee0c49003b0f"}, "language": "english", "review": "Like the first one, this game makes you feel like a power armored badass.  It's got intense battles, and the enemies are a blast to kill.\r\n\r\nThat said; I feel like the graphics, while pretty, tend to have so many glowy things that it's sometimes difficult to see what's going on.  This is less a gameplay problem, and more of a \"I can't see my character rip an alien bug's head off\" problem.\r\n\r\nThe combat is solid, the shooting and slashing, and bashing all feel good.  The only minor complaint I have is that sometimes it doesn't seem to flow.  It's a minor complaint, and sometimes I feel like I'm killing bugs left and right like in the cutscenes.", "timestamp_created": 1746661017, "timestamp_updated": 1746661017, "voted_up": true, "votes_up": 0, "votes_funny": 0, "weighted_vote_score": 0.5, "comment_count": 0, "steam_purchase": true, "received_for_free": false, "refunded": false, "written_during_early_access": false, "primarily_steam_deck": false, "app_release_date": "1725898212", "reactions": []}, {"recommendationid": "194440724", "author": {"steamid": "76561198069733233", "personaname": "Cold-Anchor", "persona_status": "offline", "profile_url": "https://steamcommunity.com/profiles/76561198069733233/", "num_games_owned": 135, "num_reviews": 11, "pl